  "strategy": "<section id=\"approach-and-rationale\">\n        <title>Gradient-Free Bayesian Optimization with Dynamic Coordination</title>\n        <p>This approach combines Bayesian optimization with functional gradient analysis using a dual-averaging scheme. Unlike previous gradient-based methods, it leverages coordinate descent with raw function evaluations rather than smooth approximations. It introduces a new covariance matrix for parameter exploration.</p>\n        <ul>\n            <li><strong>Key Innovation:</strong> Internal Bayesian forest that tracks constraint satisfaction patterns directly from score evaluations</li>\n            <li><strong>Double Correction:</strong> Automatically compares parent and sampled candidates against a validity check layer</li>\n            <li><strong>Bottleneck Solved:</strong> Escapes local minima by rebalancing between exploration and refinement phases</li>\n            <li><strong>Order Quantization:</strong> Maintains solution progress with adaptive 7-point quantile grids</li>\n        </ul>\n        <p>This method's numerical guarantee matrix ensures integral constraint satisfaction while reducing gradient noise.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section id=\"mathematical-specification\">\n        <title>Optimization Formulation</title>\n        <p>Solves:</p>\n        <pre>\nminimize&lt;n,\u03bb&gt; {\n    max_k [ \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx ] * dx\n    s.t.\n    (1) 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 \u2200x\n    (2) \u222b h(x)dx = 1\n}\n        </pre>\n        <p><strong>Variable Representation:</strong> Discretized as 425-dimensional vector h \u2208 [0,1]^425 with fixed point spacing dx = 2/425.</p>\n        <p><strong>Objective Transform:</strong> L(h) = max_k [\u0175_k] + \u03bb L2_penalty(\u2225\u2207h\u2225\u2082) where \u0175_k = w_max(\ud835\udcaa(k), \u03b2) is smooth-max transformed covariance</p>\n        <p><strong>Penalty Parameters:</strong> L2_penalty weights added dynamically for constraint enforcement as \u03bb(t) = \u03bb\u2080 + \u03b2 exp(-t/T) during optimization</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section id=\"implementation-procedure\">\n        <title>Execution Sequence</title>\n        <ol>\n            <li><strong>Initialization (4.2 seconds)</strong>\n                <code>\nstart = np.array(initial_h_values, dtype=float)\ntarget_sum = len(h) / 2.0\nh_sample = project_onto_constraint(start, target_sum)\nscore0 = evaluate_score(h_sample)\n                </code>\n            </li>\n            <li><strong>Forest Initialization (0.8s)</strong>\n                <ul>\n                    <li>Create Bayesian forest with 2 decision trees for score trends</li>\n                    <li>Randomly sample 8 points from prior uniform [0.3,0.7] and verify integration</li>\n                </ul>\n            </li>\n            <li><strong>Main Loop (1295s)</strong>\n                <table>\n                    <tr><th>Phase</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration %</th></tr>\n                    <tr><td>Exploration</td><td>Bayesian sampling</td><td>40%</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td>Operators</td><td>Gradient-free moves</td><td>20%</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td>Refinement</td><td>Smoothing layer</td><td>30%</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td>Repair</td><td>Feasibility check</td><td>10%</td></tr>\n                </table>\n            </li>\n            <li><strong>Transformation Function</strong>\n                <code>\ndef covariance_adjust(params, base_sample):\n    \u03bc = np.mean(params)\n    \u03c3 = np.std(params)\n    return max(0.7, min(1.1, base_sample * (0.9 + 0.1*sigmoid(\u03bc-0.2)) ))\n                </code>\n            </li>\n        </ol>\n    </section>\n\n    <section id=\"search-choices\">\n        <title>Search Adaptation Logic</title>\n        <p><strong>Adaptive Dimensions:</strong> Dimensions are automatically tuned between 400-600 based on gradient curvature detection</p>\n        <p><strong>Operator Schedule:</strong></p>\n        <pre>\n{\n    \"explore\": {\"new_points\": 7, \"std_multiplier\": 0.6, \n                \"threshold\": score_threshold(85.7), \"duration\": 5},\n    \"local\": {\"new_points\": 3, \"std_multiplier\": 0.6, \n             \"threshold\": score_threshold(76.4), \"duration\": 8},\n    \"refine\": {\"new_points\": 2, \"std_multiplier\": 1.4, \n              \"threshold\": score_threshold(88.9), \"duration\": 3}\n}\n        </pre>\n        <p><strong>Anomaly Detection:</strong> Monitoring score stationarity with 98-point sliding window</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section id=\"computational-budget\">\n        <title>Time Allocation Matrix</title>\n        <p><strong>Parameterized runs:</strong> Chest of drawers with 7 input banks allocated by problem scale</p>\n        <pre>\nweight_decay = [1.0e-5, 2.5e-4, 1.8e-3]  // Based on gradient variance spacing\nnum_points = [425]  // Fixed resolution for EDOs\ntime_quanta = [60,90,120]  // Budget slicing based on computation density\n        </pre>\n    </section>\n\n    <section id=\"validation-contract\">\n        <title>Candidate Validation Process</title>\n        <ol>\n            <li>Integral constraint: |\u2211h_i - 212.5| \u2264 1e-6</li>\n            <li>Bounds enforcement: 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1 \u2200i</li>\n            <li>Finite score check: np.isfinite(c5_bound)</li>\n            <li>Sanity check: c5_bound \u2264 0.38085</li>\n        </ol>\n        <p>Final solution: Revalidated using 10-fold window of score evaluations</p>\n    </section>",
